{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-0001-4000-8000-000000000001",
    "name": "Vacation",
    "description": "Postman collection for the Amit Chupak vacations backend.\n\nOne folder per controller, one request per route.\n\n### Variables\n- `base_url` — backend root URL (defaults to `http://localhost:4001`).\n- `token` — bearer token; set automatically by Register / Login.\n- `userId` — id of the logged-in user; set automatically.\n- `vacationId` — id of a vacation; set automatically by Get Vacations / Create Vacation.\n- `email`, `password` — credentials used by Register and Login. Edit these to switch between user and admin.\n\n### Admin endpoints\nThe register route always creates `role: \"User\"`. To exercise admin endpoints (create/update/delete vacation, CSV report), promote a user in MongoDB:\n```js\ndb.users.updateOne({ email: \"admin@test.com\" }, { $set: { role: \"Admin\" } });\n```\nThen set `email` / `password` to those admin credentials and run Login.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{token}}", "type": "string" }]
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://localhost:4001", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "token", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "userId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "vacationId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "email", "value": "user@test.com", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "password", "value": "User1234!", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1 - Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response has user and token', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('token').that.is.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('user');",
                  "});",
                  "if (json.token) pm.collectionVariables.set('token', json.token);",
                  "if (json.user && json.user._id) pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', json.user._id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"firstName\": \"Test\",\n  \"lastName\": \"User\",\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "auth", "register"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response has user and token', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('token').that.is.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('user');",
                  "});",
                  "if (json.token) pm.collectionVariables.set('token', json.token);",
                  "if (json.user && json.user._id) pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', json.user._id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "auth", "login"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Current User",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Returns the user record', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('_id');",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('email');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/me",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "auth", "me"]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2 - Vacations",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get Vacations",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "const list = json.vacations || json.data || (Array.isArray(json) ? json : null);",
                  "if (list && list.length > 0 && !pm.collectionVariables.get('vacationId')) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('vacationId', list[0]._id || list[0].id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/vacations?page=1&limit=9",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "vacations"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "page", "value": "1" },
                { "key": "limit", "value": "9" }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
